Standing on the precipice of the Grand Canyon at sunset, the vastness swallowed all sense of scale, and the layered rock glowed with fiery hues. A profound silence descended, broken only by the distant rush of the Colorado River far below – a testament to millennia of patient carving.  In that moment, feeling utterly small yet connected to something immense and ancient, a wave of awe washed over me, silencing thought and filling me with wonder.




